# Not published: correspondence, contact details, and generated submissions.
# papers/variants/ is rebuilt by build_variants.py, and on the author's machine
# it carries the telephone number that contact.txt supplies, so committing it
# would republish the number the source keeps out.
submission/
contact.txt
papers/variants/
papers/ssrn/
# papers/submission/ holds the assembled journal packages, including a title
# page carrying the postal address and telephone contact.txt supplies.  Same
# reason as papers/variants/: it is rebuilt by build_jfec_submission.py and
# committing it would republish what the source deliberately keeps out.
papers/submission/

# Work in progress: labs that are not yet wired into run_all.py and so have no
# stored output to be diffed against.  Shipping one would put a script in the
# repository that the reproducibility claim does not cover, and a copy of a
# wired lab sat here identical to its live twin until it was noticed, which is
# how a duplicate starts to drift.  Nothing here is published; a lab joins the
# repository by moving into labs/ with its output stored.
pending-labs/
cell_registry/
